%T A399545 42377093232,1016572168444,26498820448420,745817615588694,
%U A399545 22541664359802032,728166624058908906,25036127647724131632,912864365100667446670,35183180975362015046952,1429186799566227500001420
%N A399545 Number of unlabeled Ferrers relations on an n-element set having trivial automorphism group.
%C A399545 A relation R is Ferrers if xRy and zRw imply xRw or zRy.
%C A399545 An automorphism of R is a permutation p of the underlying set such that xRy if and only if p(x)R p(y). The relations counted here have only the identity automorphism.
%H A399545 J. Christophe, J.-P. Doignon and S. Fiorini, <a href="https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/journals/JIS/VOL6/Doignon/doignon40.html">Counting biorders</a>, Journal of Integer Sequences, Vol. 6 (2003), Article 03.4.3.
%F A399545 a(n) = Sum_{j=0..n} Sum_{p=0..j} Sum_{q=0..j} (-1)^(p+q)*binomial(j,p)*binomial(j,q)*binomial((j+1-p)*(j+1-q),n).
%F A399545 G.f.: Sum_{n>=0} a(n)*x^n = Sum_{r>=0} (1-(1+x)^(-r-1))^r.
%e A399545 For n=2, representatives of the 6 relations are {(1,1)}, {(1,2)}, {(1,1),(1,2)}, {(1,1),(2,1)}, {(1,1),(1,2),(2,1)}, and {(1,1),(1,2),(2,2)}.
%Y A399545 Cf. A399544 (all unlabeled Ferrers relations), A048163 (labeled Ferrers relations, with shifted offset).
%K A399545 nonn,new
%O A399545 0,2
